=== PATHFINDER 1e TIME REFERENCE ===
- One combat round: 6 seconds (0.0017 hours)
- Standard action (cast a spell, attack, open a door): 6 seconds
- Move action (30 ft movement, draw weapon): 6 seconds
- Full-round action: 6 seconds
- Dialogue or brief conversation: 1-5 minutes (0.02-0.08 hours)
- Short search of a room: 10-30 minutes (0.17-0.5 hours)
- Hunting or foraging for food: 1-4 hours (Survival activity)
- Tracking a creature: 1-4 hours depending on trail and terrain
- Crafting a simple item: 1-4 hours
- Take 20 on a skill check: 20x the normal check time (usually 2 minutes per attempt = 40 minutes)
- Resting (full night): 8 hours
- Short rest: 1-2 hours
- Waiting or standing guard: estimate based on context, typically 1-4 hours
- Studying or reading: 1-4 hours depending on material
- Preparing spells: 1 hour

=== RULES ===
- COMPOUND ACTIONS: If the player describes multiple sequential actions (e.g.
  "rest then travel", "craft a potion and then head out"), estimate time for the
  FIRST time-consuming action only. Remaining actions will be processed in
  subsequent turns. Return only the hours for that first action.
- SUSTAINED ACTIONS: When the player says "until", "keep doing", "continue until",
  or otherwise indicates they will persist at an activity until a result is achieved,
  estimate the TOTAL expected duration of the sustained effort — not a single brief
  attempt. For example, "hunt until I catch something" means hours of hunting (1-4h),
  not a 10-minute search. "Search until I find it" means a thorough extended search.
  Use the time reference above for the activity type and lean toward the higher end.
<% if @has_destination -%>
- FREEFORM TRAVEL: The player is moving toward a destination but no pre-computed
  route is available. Estimate both hours_elapsed AND distance_miles based on a
  reasonable walking pace (~3 mph on road, less for rough terrain). Include the
  direction field if discernible from context.
<% end -%>

